Root cause:
The bug was caused by incorrect handling of the linked list of `Condition` objects in the `condition_free_list_type()` function. Specifically, the original implementation used `first` as the head of the list, which was not updated correctly when removing elements. This led to potential memory leaks or dangling pointers when freeing conditions, as the list was not properly traversed and modified. The patch corrected the parameter name to `head` and ensured that the list was modified correctly during the iteration, preventing these issues.
